"title": "R01-R03: the first three lines of cipher on the recto",
"caption": "Lines R01 to R03 of doc. 192 recto (Archivio di Stato di Firenze, Mediceo avanti il Principato LXXII): 147 cipher signs from 192-transcription.txt, decoded by the folder’s decode.py with key.tsv. Word division is the reading’s; the cipher does not mark it. Signs marked uncertain are the declared repairs of 192-repairs.tsv: the sign 2 read b where the key gives c, the word sign read vostre, and the raised figure of trovandosi. The figures 4, 22 and 20 are code numbers; 8 and 10 are numerals. A struck sign at the end of R03 is left out.",
"unit": "cipher signs",
"key_note": "A consonant sign with the vowel as a raised figure (1 to 5 for u, o, i, e, a), bare letter signs, word signs and numbers for names. The values are those of Gabbrielli’s key no. 120 for Roberto Acciaioli, with a few fixed on the cipher letter 190 and its clear copy 191 of the same day.",
